Search eval set (P3-10, FR-15.3)

corpus.jsonl    20 invented documents, 68 chunks (heading path, pages, text); projects
                "acme" (Acme site), "beta" (Beta app) and null (the workspace knowledge
                base); "paged" says whether the document has pages.
queries.jsonl   42 queries, 14 each of kind keyword, paraphrase and mixed, with the chunk
                ids each should find.
vectors/        chunks.jsonl (one line per chunk) and queries.jsonl (one line per query):
                {"text_sha256", "model", "vector"}. A chunk is embedded as its
                context_text, the heading path and the text joined by newlines, exactly
                as knowledge indexes it; a query as its text.

How the vectors were recorded

Model:    BAAI/bge-m3 (1,024 dimensions, the slot's default model)
Date:     2026-10-01
Command:  python scripts/record_eval_vectors.py --onnx-dir <bge-m3 ONNX export> \
              --model BAAI/bge-m3
          (run from backend/, with onnxruntime 1.30, tokenizers and numpy installed in
          the interpreter; none of them is a backend dependency)

The vectors come from the model's ONNX export on CPU (the export's sentence_embedding
output, the CLS vector, L2-normalised, rounded to 6 decimals), because no vLLM was
reachable from the build machine. The homelab check re-records them through the real
endpoint with the same script:

    uv run python scripts/record_eval_vectors.py --endpoint http://<vllm host>:8000/v1 \
        --model BAAI/bge-m3 --dims 1024

The embeddings fake (FakeEmbeddings(recorded=...)) looks vectors up by the SHA-256 of the
exact text and raises on a miss, so a changed chunker fails a test instead of silently
dropping a chunk from the vector list.
